    "image_with_text_YGEHyN": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_3UjAjz": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading_text": "Why do ATC partner growers outperform the average grower?",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "enable_h1_tag": false
          }
        },
        "description_fBwmjn": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p>Most techniques that work in Europe cannot simply be copied for use in North America. Our microclimates, soil chemistry, and—critically—the soil biome (the organisms interacting with truffle fungi) are fundamentally different. On top of that, unlike conventional crops like grapes or corn, actionable truffle science is largely absent from the public domain.</p><p>Through our own research, we’ve developed region-specific truffle science that is available only to ATC partner growers. Armed with this otherwise unavailable knowledge, our growers consistently outperform the average by a wide margin. Just as importantly, we provide ongoing leadership and proactive guidance, rather than waiting for problems to arise as in a typical consulting model. </p>"
          }
        },
        "button_CG8QhP": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_primary_label": "Our Technology",
            "button_primary_style": "primary",
            "button_primary_link": "shopify://pages/our-technology",
            "button_secondary_label": "",
            "button_secondary_style": "secondary",
            "button_secondary_link": "shopify://pages/truffle-fundamentals"
          }
        }
      },
